NXR-151|Opt-in bounded stack watermark observations|Metrics|The kernel shall provide opt-in boot stack painting and explicit budgeted stack observations without adding per-thread storage or scanning in scheduling paths.|Measured observations support stack budgeting without confusing paint with a guaranteed free-space proof.|Paint before context creation; scan at most floor(budget_bytes/4) words plus a separate guard check; reject unregistered identities without output mutation; report disabled and incomplete observations explicitly; cover bounds and ARM worker stacks.|Host scanner boundary matrix, ARM real-stack observations, no-heap audit and feature-off cross-build.|NXR-150|RTOS_STACK_WATERMARK defaults off; explicit stack_usage scan budget defaults to 256 bytes.|No target heap and no new thread-control fields; constant result storage; scan work bounded by caller budget and registered extent.|include/rtos/detail/stack_watermark.hpp,include/rtos.hpp,include/rtos_config.hpp,src/kernel.cpp,tests/stack_watermark.cpp,examples/arm_stress.cpp,docs/metrics.rst|Watermark scans are separate from ordinary snapshots and dispatch. Paint collisions and unwritten reserved frames remain documented limits; full scans require an explicit interrupt-latency allowance.|include/rtos/detail/stack_watermark.hpp,src/kernel.cpp,tests/stack_watermark.cpp,examples/arm_stress.cpp|tests/stack_watermark.cpp,examples/arm_stress.cpp|PartialSourceUnverified
